    "batching_and_compression": "Thousands of transactions are compressed and bundled into batches. Only cryptographic state differences and validity proofs are posted upstream, reducing network congestion and minimizing gas fees by over 95% compared to native L1 transfers.",
    "proof_generation_latency": "To prevent proving bottlenecks, Merlin Chain utilizes Lumoz's specialized decentralized ZK-PoW mining infrastructure, allowing distributed hardware nodes (GPUs) to compute SNARK/STARK proofs concurrently, accelerating state confirmation times.",
    "finality_stages": "Users experience instant 'soft finality' via the sequencer layer for everyday DeFi and dApp interactions, while 'hard finality' is achieved after batch settlement and Taproot commitment on the Bitcoin base layer."
  },
  "security_impact": {
    "cryptographic_validity": "Unlike optimistic rollups that rely on a 7-day challenge window and fraud proofs, ZK rollups guarantee that invalid state transitions are mathematically impossible to commit. The sequencer cannot forge user balances or steal funds without generating an invalid proof.",
    "bitcoin_l1_anchoring": "Merlin periodically commits aggregated state roots and zero-knowledge validity proofs to Bitcoin L1 using Taproot scripts, ensuring state immutability backed by Bitcoin's proof-of-work security.",
